--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@ package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.
 ### Fixed
 
 - `onError` and `afterSession` hooks now fire when `beforeSession` throws, matching the guarantee the hook names imply. Previously, a throw from `beforeSession` escaped the `try`/`finally` block entirely, so neither hook ran. **Migration note**: if your `afterSession` hook assumed it would only be called after a full session turn, it will now also be called when `beforeSession` itself fails — the hook can inspect the session to detect this case (no entries beyond the initial user message will have been processed).
+- `onError` now fires for a rejection that is not an `Error`. The hook receives an `Error` whose `message` carries the thrown value (the string itself, or JSON for any other value) and whose `cause` holds the original, so a hook typed against `Error` keeps compiling and one that wants the raw rejection reads `cause`; the value the caller's promise rejects with is unchanged. **Migration note**: an `onError` that alerts or writes incident records now fires for rejections it never saw — a provider that rejects with a string, a plain object or `undefined` previously bypassed the hook entirely, so anything it counted was under-counted.
 
